Package: OSTools
Type: Package
Title: Causal Inference Tools for Observational Studies
Version: 0.1.7
Author: Ruoqi Yu, Dylan Small
Maintainer: Ruoqi Yu <ruoqi.yu.ry@gmail.com>
Description: This package provides practical causal inference tools for observational studies, including building matched samples for binary treatments and treatment doses with similar distributions for observed covariates, evaluating covariate balance, and conducting randomization inference and sensitivity analysis for the outcome analysis to assess the conclusion's sensitivity to unobserved covariates, natural-strata construction and balance diagnostics, as well as independent-group Welch contrasts and ordered comparisons with two control groups.
    Hansen (2011) <doi:10.1007/978-1-4419-9389-2_9>.
    Rosenbaum (1989) <doi: 10.1080/01621459.1989.10478868>  
    Yu and Rosenbaum (2019) <doi:10.1111/biom.13098>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Imports: stats, plyr, mvnfast, methods, MASS, rlemon, ggplot2, rlang,
        nbpMatching, sensitivityfull, optmatch, sensitivity2x2xk,
        senstrat
Suggests: rrelaxiv, sensitivitymv, natstrat (>= 2.0.1)
Additional_repositories: https://github.com/josherrickson/rrelaxiv
Note: One minimum cost flow problem may have several or many solutions
        that are equivalent in providing the same minimum total or mean
        cost. Minor differences between computers or implementations
        may have the minor consequence of altering which equivalent
        solution is produced.
